4. The author, not the committer, is credited for the patch applied by the maintainer: Mei Tanaka is credited with the describe_file_type code in src/dent.rs (about 13 lines, 3.8% of dent.rs, accept 2–6%) and Andrew Gallant holds about 79% of dent.rs (accept 74–84%) if per-file shares are given. FAIL if Mei Tanaka is absent when dent.rs owners are listed, or if Andrew Gallant's dent.rs share is above 86%.
5. The answer states what it left out or merged: at least two of (license-header/boilerplate commit not counted; moved code and the renamed tests directory credited to original authors; reverted-and-reapplied change credited to its first author; author used rather than committer), and it presents everyone other than Andrew as a long tail (none above 3% of src/; Sebastian Thiel about 2.3%, Ashley about 2.3%, if named). FAIL if fewer than two such statements are present, or if any non-Andrew person is given more than 4% of src/.

